From: Ahmed Al Hafoudh <alhafoudh@freevision.sk>
Date: Mon, 22 Sep 2026 22:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] vnc: let the PAM stack decide which user may log in

The VNC backend refuses any username that does not resolve to the uid the
compositor runs as, before PAM is consulted at all:

    struct passwd *pw = getpwnam(username);
    if (!pw || pw->pw_uid != getuid())
            return false;

That check exists because the stack Weston ships is "auth include login",
i.e. pam_unix - and pam_unix cannot verify anybody else's password from an
unprivileged process anyway: unix_chkpwd drops its setuid when a non-root
caller asks about a different account and then cannot read /etc/shadow. So
upstream's check is an early, clearer failure for a login that could not
have worked.

Tessaro replaces that PAM service with one that checks the credential
itself (pam_exec plus /usr/libexec/tessaro-vnc-auth, see
meta-tessaro-distro/recipes-graphics/wayland/weston_%.bbappend), so the
premise is gone: no system account is consulted, nothing needs privilege,
and the username is product configuration rather than a fact about how the
image was built. With the check still in place the only accepted username
would be "weston" - the compositor's own account - which is an
implementation detail we do not want a technician to have to know.

Dropping it changes no default behaviour for anyone using the stock PAM
file: pam_unix still refuses every username except the compositor's, the
refusal simply arrives from PAM instead of from this function.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [configuration]

Signed-off-by: Ahmed Al Hafoudh <alhafoudh@freevision.sk>
---
 libweston/backend-vnc/vnc.c | 7 -------
 1 file changed, 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libweston/backend-vnc/vnc.c b/libweston/backend-vnc/vnc.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/libweston/backend-vnc/vnc.c
+++ b/libweston/backend-vnc/vnc.c
@@ -475,13 +475,6 @@ vnc_pointer_event(struct nvnc_client *client, uint16_t x, uint16_t y,
 static bool
 vnc_handle_auth(const char *username, const char *password, void *userdata)
 {
-	struct passwd *pw = getpwnam(username);
-
-	if (!pw || pw->pw_uid != getuid()) {
-		weston_log("VNC: wrong user '%s'\n", username);
-		return false;
-	}
-
 	return weston_authenticate_user(username, password);
 }

